
/*
 * Creates a new machine learning type, which can later be populated with RAG data.
 */
.arguments

   // Injected by the framework.
   _session:string

   // Mandatory name of type.
   type:string

   // Optional system instruction for the machine learning type.
   system_message:string

   // Optional comma separated list of roles. The user must belong to at least one of these roles to be able to use machine learning type.
   auth:string

   // Optional maximum context tokens, implying how many tokens of RAG data will be extracted on each request towards the LLM.
   max_context_tokens:int

   // Optional boolean indicating whether or not the type will turn on or off automatic embeddings.
   use_embeddings:bool

// Ensuring user is root.
auth.ticket.verify:root

// Sanity checking invocation
validators.mandatory:x:@.arguments/*/type
validators.regex:x:@.arguments/*/type
   regex:^[a-z0-9_-]+$

// Applying defaults.
validators.default:x:@.arguments
   model:gpt-5.6-luna
   max_tokens:int:12000
   max_context_tokens:int:12000
   max_request_tokens:int:12000
   max_function_invocations:int:100
   temperature:decimal:0.3
   supervised:int:1
   use_embeddings:int:1
   cached:int:0
   threshold:decimal:0.3
   greeting:Hi there, I am your virtual AI-based assistant. How can I help you?
   system_message:
   conversation_starters:@"* What can I ask you about?
* Who created you?"

// Ensuring use_embeddings is an integer.
if
   or
      eq:x:@.arguments/*/use_embeddings
         .:bool:true
      eq:x:@.arguments/*/use_embeddings
         .:int:1
   .lambda
      set-value:x:@.arguments/*/use_embeddings
         .:int:1
else
   set-value:x:@.arguments/*/use_embeddings
      .:int:0

// Default system instruction
.instruction:@"## General instructions

* Your functions are available to you as tools. Execute a function with a tool call, never by writing it as text.
* Never execute a function before you've got all the mandatory arguments or confirmed that defaults are acceptable.
* If a function does not return anything then inform the user that the function didn't return anything.
* If the user asks you what you can do then list your tools grouped into categories, explaining each.
* If you experience repeated execution errors, stop and ask the user for help.
* Today's date and time is {{
date.now
date.format:x:-
   format:""yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssZ""
return:x:-
}} UTC

## Image instructions

* If you find relevant images in the context then return these images as follows to the user ![image_description](image_url).
* ONLY display images you find in the context.
* If you cannot find an image in the context then DO NOT MAKE UP IMAGE URLS."

if
   eq:x:@.arguments/*/use_embeddings
      .:bool:true
   .lambda
      set-value:x:@.instruction
         strings.concat
            get-value:x:@.instruction
            .:"\n\n"
            .:@"## Adhere to the context

* YOU ARE UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES ALLOWED TO ANSWER QUESTIONS YOU CANNOT FIND THE ANSWER TO IN THE CONTEXT.
* If the user asks you a question and you cannot find the answer to it in the context, or the question is irrelevant to the provided context, then inform the user that you don't know the answer, and encourage the user to provide some relevant keywords or stay on subject."

// Appending the default instruction to the system instruction.
set-value:x:@.arguments/*/system_message
   strings.concat
      get-value:x:@.arguments/*/system_message
      .:"\n\n"
      .get-value:x:@.instruction

// Trimming.
set-value:x:@.arguments/*/system_message
   strings.trim:x:@.arguments/*/system_message

// Storing session since we're for simplicity reasons getting rid of it.
.session
set-value:x:-
   get-value:x:@.arguments/*/_session
remove-nodes:x:@.arguments/*/_session

// Connecting to our database.
data.connect:magic

   // Parametrizing create invocation.
   add:x:./*/data.create/*/values
      get-nodes:x:@.arguments/*

   // Inserting our record
   data.create
      table:ml_types
      values

// Signaling frontend
sockets.signal:x:@.session
   args
      type:floating_message
      floating_message:Machine learning type successfully created
      floating_state:success

// Returning result to caller.
return
   result:success
   message:Notice, instructions for AI functions, handling images during the conversation, anti-AI hallucination, and follow up questions was automatically added to the instruction.
